Calculated;\n```\n\nIn the transformed query, we\'ve moved the MIN function calls outside of the original query and stored the results in a temporary table (PreCalculated). This allows the database to optimize the repeated calculations and reduce execution time."""'}], 'response': "Here is a summary of the provided SQL query rewrite strategies:\n\nThe given SQL query can be rewritten using three different strategies. The first strategy applies Case 1 of the query rewrite rule, which directly applies aggregate functions (`MIN`) and joins tables without any transformations or additional expressions. This transformation does not alter the expected result set and preserves the semantics of the original query. The second strategy moves filter conditions that can be logically associated with columns from one side of an INNER JOIN into the ON clause of the JOIN or as a WHERE clause on a subquery of the respective side, reducing the size of the datasets before the join occurs. The third strategy applies Rule 1's transformation 3 by storing the result in a variable or temporary table when using aggregate functions that are called multiple times with the same parameters. This allows the database to optimize repeated calculations and reduce execution time.", 'time': 1.7651493549346924}
